+# GEO Workbench architecture — v0.2.1
 
-The export adds a Node HTTP/auth adapter and a SQLite repository at `src/server`. It reuses the domain and application services. Root npm commands now target React/Vite + Node, while the D1 and Sites route source remain as references. A complete unmodified hosted source snapshot is under `reference/GEO_Workbench_Sites_Source.tar.gz`.
+The standalone product is a modular monolith: React/Vite UI, a Node 24 HTTP composition root, application services, a framework-free domain core, and replaceable infrastructure adapters. SQLite supports one local machine or single VM. The exact earlier hosted React/Vinext + Worker/D1 edition is archived in `reference/`.
 
-Local identity is a configured owner with loopback-only binding. Cloud identity uses one configured Basic-auth user behind Caddy HTTPS. Organization membership, OIDC/SSO and enterprise roles remain future work. The original hosting-specific identity assumptions below apply only to the original Sites runtime. See `SETUP.md` and `VALIDATION.md` for portable setup and completed checks.
+## Dependency boundaries
 
----
